---
const steps = [
  ['Choose the specialist','Enter Agent Workforce and select the Compliance Agent whose capability matches the work.'],
  ['Inspect the template','Open the PCI-compliance job and review its timeline, expected outcomes, schedule and approval model.'],
  ['Start deliberately','Run the job only after its scope, trigger, timing and “always ask for approval” boundary are understood.'],
  ['Monitor the reasoning','Follow the agent through template review, reporting, remediation, verification and documentation.'],
  ['Watch when useful','Use live UI changes to observe the agent working without turning supervision into permanent screen-staring.'],
  ['Verify the finish','Review updated reports, audit logs and change details before accepting the job as complete.'],
];

const controls = [
  ['Pause remediation','Interrupt the work when the evidence or operating context changes.'],
  ['Ask the assistant','Question the agent inside the job instead of leaving the workflow to reconstruct context.'],
  ['Review details','Expand completed and active steps to inspect rules, actions and reasoning.'],
  ['Follow live changes','Observe the agent’s interface activity when direct visibility adds confidence.'],
  ['Download evidence','Retrieve reports, audit logs and rule references for accountable closure.'],
];
---

<div class="manage-journey">
  <header class="manage-hero">
    <a href="/work/agenticops#agentic-trust">← Back to Trust journey</a>
    <p>Journey 04 · Manage a job in Agent Workforce</p>
    <h1>Delegate the work. Keep the judgment.</h1>
    <div><p>An operator can create and monitor a compliance job without surrendering control. The journey makes the agent’s remit, progress, evidence and intervention points visible from setup to closure.</p><aside>Phase 02 · AgenticOps<br/><b>Delegation without disappearance</b></aside></div>
  </header>

  <nav aria-label="Manage-job journey chapters"><a href="#flow">Job lifecycle</a><a href="#controls">Operator controls</a><a href="#artifact">Figma artifact</a><a href="#contract">Trust contract</a></nav>

  <section id="flow" class="manage-section">
    <p class="index">01 / Job lifecycle</p><h2>Six moves from choosing an agent to accepting its evidence.</h2>
    <div class="step-grid">{steps.map(([title,copy],index) => <article><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section id="controls" class="manage-section dark-section">
    <p class="index">02 / Operator controls</p><h2>Supervision is designed into the work—not bolted on when something feels odd.</h2>
    <p class="lead">The job remains interrogable and interruptible while the agent is running. Progress is useful; progress with a pause button is considerably more relaxing.</p>
    <div class="control-list">{controls.map(([title,copy],index) => <article><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><strong>{title}</strong><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div>
    <aside>The agent owns execution. The operator retains authority, context and the final word.</aside>
  </section>

  <section id="artifact" class="manage-section artifact-section">
    <p class="index">03 / Complete Figma artifact</p><h2>The complete Agent Workforce journey, preserved exactly as designed.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Scroll from specialist selection and job configuration through active remediation, live-change observation, completion evidence and audit-ready outputs.</p>
    <figure><img src="/images/agentic-journeys/agentic-manage-job-flow-2025-6.png" alt="Complete AgenticOps journey for creating and monitoring a PCI compliance job in Agent Workforce" loading="eager" /><figcaption><span>2025-6 · Journey artifact</span><p>Exact export from the supplied Figma artboard. The Cisco interface screens remain unchanged.</p></figcaption></figure>
  </section>

  <section id="contract" class="manage-section contract-section">
    <p class="index">04 / Trust contract</p><h2>A managed job keeps permission, progress and proof connected.</h2>
    <div class="contract-flow"><article><span>Permission</span><b>Choose the specialist, scope, schedule and approval behavior</b></article><i>→</i><article><span>Progress</span><b>See current steps, reasoning and live operational changes</b></article><i>→</i><article><span>Proof</span><b>Review reports, change logs and documented outcomes</b></article></div>
    <div class="journey-footer"><a href="/work/agenticops/journeys/bulk-assign-insights">← Previous · Bulk assignment</a><a href="/work/agenticops#agentic-trust">All journeys</a><a href="/work/agenticops/journeys/configure-agent">Next · Configure an agent →</a></div>
  </section>
</div>

